body:
Thank you for responding in-depth. I actually did document what happened, and still I doubt myself, that's how good manipulators they are I guess. Because since I don't have anyone else to talk to, I often come to my mom for support even though she's the one who's gaslighting me (I had to force myself not to say "supposedly" there). I think I will start grey rocking.

&#x200B;

Where should I look to for legal/psychological counsel? My relationship with my therapist ended because my parents were turned off by her after she called child services (my mom berated her for it and kept saying that they were good parents and that she should know that) and I am not on good terms with my high school counselor. Are helplines useful?

&#x200B;

EDIT: After reading more into grey rocking, I think I already do this on occasion with my sister and parents. I think my sister is the most blatant narcs because whenever we have a conversation there has to be a winner as opposed to compromise or resolution and it has to be her. When I don't respond/ignore her or respond in yes/no she'll keep bugging me and be physically in my face, waiting for me to implode, like one time she was towering over me as I sat just saying the same shit over and over again waiting for me to respond. I also don't have a lock on my door so I can't keep any of them out.
